From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: acqxi <kacqxi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:07:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Performance metrics: composer, per-reply history and
 settings

Stats for nerds turn performance in the web UI, coded against the
OrchestrationV2TurnPerformance contract.

- TurnPerformance.logic.ts: one provider turn -> metric rows (ttft, ttfa,
  liveTps, avgTps, peakTps, tokens, cache hit rate, context, tool time,
  turn time, provider, model, effort, speed), each exact / estimated /
  unavailable with a tooltip reason. avgTps uses generation windows only
  (exact only for provider_exact), legacy responseThroughput only under
  its own label. Client-side live tokens/s sampler (2 s window, keyed by
  thread + provider turn).
- Composer: a line under the stats line with the running turn (elapsed,
  live tok/s, TTFT/TTFA) and the previous completed turn, each with a
  full breakdown on hover. The stats line hands its tok/s and cache chips
  to this line when it is shown.
- Timeline: a one-line footer under each reply for the provider turn that
  produced it, with the breakdown on hover.
- Settings: Stats for nerds moves to General, with switches for composer,
  per-reply and each metric (statsForNerdsHiddenMetrics), reset buttons
  and search entries. New catalog keys in every web locale.
